      "math_academy_id": "e-7171",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14234521/assets/dcddc9ee6fe49965ea4f261fcb43c6f7ccd14193910e864b950745ef513e67a6.png)\n\nThe sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ are shown in the Venn diagram above. Find $X\\cup Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "The union $X \\cup Y$ consists of all the elements that are in $X$ or $Y,$ or both. To represent $X \\cup Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained within either $X$ or $Y,$ or both.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14234521/assets/c94cfc38872dfe0673e112e09feec7781ab4f247f08932d1d8ecd167b4a99d32.png)\n\nThe elements $1,2,3,4,5,8$ are in either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. Therefore, the union of $X$ and $Y$ is\n\n$$\nX \\cup Y = \\{ 1,2,3,4,5,8 \\}.\n$$",
